date A and D fully. We need to bring them in perhaps, but must connect to prior discussion. We can either maintain vote for C, or shift. We have evidence for C strong. We could bring up A and D to compare, but ensure we are not just dumping facts. We can say we still support C, but note that A and D have concerns that make them less suitable. Provide explicit facts: A can anticipate dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership qualities, but regarded as show\u2011off, not open to new ideas, unorganized, not good at taking criticism. D responds adequately to unexpected events, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, but regarded as know\u2011it\u2011all, hot temper, moody, loner, weak leadership. Use these to argue C remains best.\n\nThus produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE: I agree with Agent 1 and 3, keep C, note A and D concerns. Provide evidence. Then METADATA_JSON vote Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
